    {
      "id": "41837b2ce4d8c926917519e23510b6ba2735f480",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 813278056,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi. This is the fix I was going to push, it shuts up the warnings for sure. I stopped because I wanted to be sure the dissection was as expected. An example of uninitialized path (before this patch)\n\n```c\n2843: ptp_frame_info_t *frame_info;\n2844: switch (ptp_v2_messageid)\n...\n======> missing \"else\", so no branch is taken and frame info is undefined.\n2886: if PTP_FRAME_INFO_SYNC_COMPLETE(frame_info) {    <=== using frame info with undefined value\n```\n\nThe fix is to initialize `frame_info` with `NULL`. Is that ok then to call line 2886 with NULL from a dissection perspective? (Yes, it is, since PTP_FRAME_INFO_SYNC_COMPLETE starts with (fi) != NULL, but I took the easier example as reference).\n\nSo the question is: are the zeros valid values when used in the dissection? If so, the patch is good.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-18T07:50:21.437Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-18T07:50:21.437Z",
